	)
	(text "For any connector or exposed interface\nyou typically should add ESD protection\nto make sure when you're messing around\nwith the board you don't accidentally\nfry your devices.\nHowever, phil says that from his experience\nthese ST mcus are pretty resilient, so\nit's fine for *test boards* to skip them, however\nhe doesn't recommend this for connectors\non commercial boards"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.366 90.424 0)
		(effects
